*.swp
*~

# Claude Code session settings — NEITHER file is committed (Mike ruled
# 2026-07-29, option ⓑ: untrack everywhere, one uniform rule). The allowlist
# names the commands a session runs UNPROMPTED; published, it maps an agent's
# unattended reach for anyone who can open an issue or a PR. A
# visibility-conditional rule would silently become wrong the day a repo flips,
# so the rule does not depend on visibility. Seed a new clone from
# docs/build/templates/claude/settings.json.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Harness-native worktrees land here — a sibling session's live worktree is
# NOT ours to commit (CONCURRENCY § Stay in your lane); never track its gitlink.
.claude/worktrees/

